  "final_text": "I finished all four steps, using only the Kibana tools.\n\n1. **Data view:** The 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' data view (index `kibana_sample_data_flights`) has 33 fields, including `Carrier`, `Cancelled` (boolean) and `FlightDelayMin`. Its time field is `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** I created 'S4-19a11fc6 Flights' with exactly two panels: a line chart of the number of flights over time, and a bar chart of the number of flights for each of the top 10 carriers.\n3. **Alert rule:** I created 'S4-19a11fc6 Cancelled flights' as an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 flights with `Cancelled: true` arrive within 5 minutes. I created it already enabled, so I didn't need to turn it on separately.\n4. **Edit and read-back:** I renamed the carrier panel to 'Flights by carrier', and reading the dashboard back shows the new title. Reading the rule back shows it is enabled and its status is \"ok\".\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, so when it fires it won't send notifications anywhere.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
